      }
    ],
    "bottomLine": "If you get fewer than 100 calls/month and don't need CRM integration or real-time booking, a traditional service works fine. For growing businesses that need every lead captured, qualified, and booked \u2014 AI wins on cost, consistency, and capability.",
    "bestFor": {
      "a": "Very low call volume businesses, businesses requiring exclusively human interaction",
      "b": "Service businesses, medical/dental practices, law firms, any business losing leads to voicemail"
    },
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "Can an AI receptionist really replace a human?",
        "a": "For 90% of inbound calls \u2014 yes. AI handles scheduling, qualification, routing, and FAQs better than most answering service operators. For complex emotional situations (counseling, crisis), human operators still have an edge."
